[TEST] Perform targeted physical examination:  
- Assess for nuchal rigidity (passive neck flexion) and Brudzinski/Kernig signs;  
- Fundoscopic exam for papilledema or retinal hemorrhages;  
- Skin exam for rash, petechiae, or purpura;  
- Palpate cervical, axillary, and inguinal lymph nodes for enlargement or tenderness;  
- Brief neurologic screen: mental status (orientation ×3), cranial nerves II–XII (focusing on visual fields, extraocular movements, facial symmetry, tongue deviation), and motor strength in upper/lower extremities (5/5 bilaterally).

